DAY 20 — FILE TRANSFER: SCP & RSYNC
Commands Reference Sheet
Machine: Kali Linux | User: raven
==========================================

--- SCP (quick, simple transfers) ---
scp file.txt user@host:/path/           # send a file TO remote machine
scp user@host:/path/file.txt .           # pull a file FROM remote machine
scp -r folder/ user@host:/path/          # copy an entire folder (needs -r)
scp -P 2222 file.txt user@host:/path/    # use a custom SSH port

--- RSYNC — BASIC SYNC ---
rsync -av source/ destination/           # local sync, archive mode + verbose
rsync -avz source/ user@host:/path/      # sync over SSH, with compression

--- RSYNC — KEY FLAGS ---
-a    # archive mode — preserves permissions, timestamps, symlinks
-v    # verbose — show what's happening
-z    # compress data during transfer
--progress    # show a progress bar per file
--dry-run     # PREVIEW changes without actually transferring anything

--- RSYNC — SAFE PREVIEW BEFORE A REAL SYNC ---
rsync -avz --dry-run source/ user@host:/path/     # see what WOULD happen

--- RSYNC — MIRRORING (removes extra files in destination) ---
rsync -avz --delete source/ destination/          # DANGEROUS — always --dry-run first!
rsync -avz --dry-run --delete source/ destination/  # safe preview of a --delete sync

--- RSYNC — EXCLUDING FILES ---
rsync -avz --exclude="*.log" source/ dest/         # skip .log files
rsync -avz --exclude="temp/" source/ dest/          # skip a specific subfolder
rsync -avz --exclude="*.log" --exclude="temp/" source/ dest/  # multiple excludes

--- TRAILING SLASH RULE (important!) ---
rsync -av folder/ dest/     # copies CONTENTS of folder into dest
rsync -av folder dest/      # copies the FOLDER ITSELF into dest (creates dest/folder/)

